    {
      "id": "1",
      "title": "Situation overview",
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "1a",
          "title": "Overview",
          "bullets": [
            {
              "id": "1a.1",
              "text": "A mining-region landslide in Dreth damaged the lower road and disrupted services at Corvane mine and surrounding benches. Evacuations affected approximately 60 households from Withel terraces and Cranmoor, with displacement reported across multiple areas. Information updates were provided about tailings ponds and dams, while community support was organized in Withel terraces and policy revisions were announced by Yelverton Minerals and an independent panel.",
              "confidence": "confirmed",
              "tweet_ids": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "title": "Timeline",
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "2a",
          "title": "Chronological timeline",
          "bullets": [
            {
              "id": "2a.1",
              "text": "On 2026-03-14, a warning was issued for Withel terraces and Cranmoor, followed by evacuation of about 60 households from Withel terraces and people from Cranmoor; the lower road was damaged by the slide. On 2026-03-16, service disruptions were reported in Ashfell bench and upper bench, with evacuations from the bench. On 2026-03-17, damage occurred in Dreth and the Pellan, information was provided about tailings pond and dam, and service at Corvane mine and the pit was disrupted. On 2026-03-18, service at the pit remained disrupted. On 2026-03-19, 60 households were displaced from Cranmoor, service at the lower road was disrupted then restored, service was restored in Dreth and the Pellan, community support was organized in Withel terraces, and Yelverton Minerals and an independent panel revised its policy.",
